        <detaileddescription>
<para>detects the format from file extension and saves the raster in it Generated from function <computeroutput>MR::RasterSave::toAnySupportedFormat</computeroutput>. Parameter <computeroutput>raster</computeroutput> can not be null. It is a single object. Parameter <computeroutput>path</computeroutput> is a UTF-8 encoded filesystem path. Parameter <computeroutput>settings</computeroutput> is a single object. Parameter <computeroutput>settings</computeroutput> has a default argument: <computeroutput>{}</computeroutput>, pass a null pointer to use it. Never returns null. Returns an instance allocated on the heap! Must call <computeroutput><ref refid="expected__void__std__string_8h_1a9638e07d2c5281b4bf574c618ab6f2e9" kindref="member">MR_expected_void_std_string_Destroy()</ref></computeroutput> to free it when you&apos;re done using it. </para>
